  "status": "PROVED H4 STRENGTHENING: PRIMITIVE CANONICAL ORBITS INJECT INTO O(n^2) INTERVAL WITNESSES",
  "task": "X75 h=4 witness-injection bound",
  "theorem": "Every primitive h=4 X64 canonical row orbit has an X64 transform with odd first exponent d.  Scaling that transform by d^{-1} gives a normalized interval word which vanishes at the primitive root zeta^d.  For fixed d, interval sign, and interval length, X71's geometric-series equation forces the interval start if it exists. Choosing the lexicographically first such witness gives an injection from primitive canonical row orbits into at most 2*phi(n)*(n-1)=n(n-1)<n^2 witnesses."
